{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user provided a complex automated \"stitch\" task (Task ID 5180) from a cobbler orchestrator work queue. The task is to implement srd005-wc requirements R1.1 through R1.4 in the go-unix-utils project, which is a Go reimplementation of GNU coreutils verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The specific requirements are:\n   - R1.1: When no flags given, print line count, word count, and byte count (in that order) for each input\n   - R1.2: Read from stdin when no file arguments; read from each named file in order when file arguments given\n   - R1.3: Output for each file on a single line with counts followed by filename; no filename for stdin\n   - R1.4: When more than one file given, print a final \"total\" line with sum of all counts\n   \n   Design decisions mandate: preserve existing R2.1-R2.6 and R3.1-R3.2 functionality, follow differential testing pattern with gwc, ensure SIGPIPE handler is called.\n\n   Acceptance criteria: R1.1-R1.4 implemented in main.go, differential tests pass against gwc, existing tests still pass, `go build ./cmd/wc/` succeeds, `go test ./cmd/wc/ -count=1` passes.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against GNU reference binary (gwc)\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - GNU wc behavior: default mode prints lines, words, bytes; column-aligned output; \"total\" line for multi-file\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for locale-independent testing\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` to compile the binary under test\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gwc\")` with `t.Skip` for graceful skip when reference binary absent\n   - No git co