ests` pattern\n     - `defaultEnv = []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}`\n     - `TestDiff` - 35 stdin-based differential tests covering flags, combinations, empty input, binary input\n     - `TestDiffFiles` - 9 file-based differential tests covering multi-file, single file, various flag combinations\n     - Has `writeFixture` helper for creating test files\n     - Already has tests like \"default_no_flags\", \"empty_input\", \"multi_file_default\", \"multi_file_three_files\", \"single_file_no_total\" that appear to cover R1.1-R1.4\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD specification and existing code to understand what R1.1-R1.4 require\n   - Analyzed the existing implementation and found that the core R1.1-R1.4 functionality appears to already be present in the codebase\n   - The task states R2.1-R2.6 and R3.1-R3.2 are \"already implemented\" but R1.1-R1.4 need to be added, despite the code apparently having this functionality\n   - Need to determine if there are subtle gaps in R1.1-R1.4 coverage or if additional test cases are needed\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The complete task specification including role description, repository files list, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements R1-R4, design decisions D1-D3, acceptance criteria AC1-AC5, shared protocols, and package contracts. This is an automated stitch task from the cobbler orchestrator.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Requesting a detailed summary of the conversation, with analysis block followed by summary block.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Analyze gaps between existing R1.1-R1.4 implementation and what the SRD requires\n   - Add any missing R1.1-R1.4 functionality to cmd/wc/main.go\n   - Add differential test cases specifically targeting R1.1-R1.4 to cmd/wc/wc_test.go  \n   - Run `go build -o bin/wc ./cmd/wc/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/wc/ -count=1` to verify all tests pass\n   - Verify all 5 acceptance criteria (AC1-AC5) are met\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the three required files (SRD, main.go, wc_test.go) and was about to begin the implementation phase. I had not yet made any code changes. My analysis showed that the existing code in cmd/wc/main.go appears to already implement R1.1-R1.4 core functionality (default no-flags behavior, stdin/file reading, per-file output format, total line). The existing tests also appear to cover these scenarios. I need to determine precisely what is missing and add it.\n\n   The task description says: \"Add functionality for srd005-wc R1.1-R1.4\" to main.go and \"Add differential test cases for R1.1-R1.4\" to wc_test.go. Given the existing code already handles these, I may need to:\n   1. Verify there are no edge case gaps\n   2. Add explicitly labeled R1.1-R1.4 test cases (e.g., testing stdin-with-no-filename, testing file args read in order, testing total line specifically)\n   3. Perhaps add test cases for R1.2's \"read from each named file in order\" and R1.3's \"no filename for stdin\" and R1.4's total line edge cases\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   The immediate next step is to implement the task. Since the existing code appears to largely cover R1.1-R1.4, I should:\n   1. Verify the existing implementation is fully correct for R1.1-R1.4 (check edge cases like: stdin showing no filename, file arguments processed in order, total line sum correctness)\n   2. Add any missing test cases explicitly covering R1.1-R1.4 scenarios to wc_test.go - particularly file-based tests that verify R1.2 (files read in order), R1.3 (filename in output), and R1.4 (total line with sums)\n   3. Run build and tests to verify AC1-AC5\n\n   From the task: \"requirements: R1: Implement srd005-wc R1.1 as s